Package: gnome-shell-extension-xiws
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         gnome-shell (>= 48~),
         gnome-shell (<< 49~)
Description: dev workspaces for GNOME Shell
 Opens and switches project sessions from a searchable picker in the panel.
 A workspace bundles a project directory with the applications belonging to
 it: the editor, a browser window and the git client.
 .
 The version bounds on gnome-shell are deliberate. GNOME Shell breaks
 extension API compatibility between major releases, so the package refuses
 to stay installed across an unverified shell upgrade.

Package: chrome-extension-xiws
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: google-chrome-stable
Description: chrome counterpart to the xiws workspace picker
 Persists the tabs of a Chrome window per xiws workspace and restores them
 when that workspace is opened again. The durable copy lives in bookmarks,
 so it travels with the Chrome account.
 .
 The extension is registered through a preferences file under
 /usr/share/google-chrome/extensions, which is how Chrome picks up a locally
 installed extension on Linux without a store listing or an update server.
 Chrome itself is only recommended, since the package is equally usable with
 another channel of the browser.
